WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.700
OK, so we're continuing to talk about testing
and Donald Trump has now confirmed that he

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.720
was not kidding when he said slow down Corona
virus testing.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:17.170
The White House has been tripping all over
itself for days to say Trump was just joking.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.560
Trump was then asked, were you joking?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.339
And he said, I don't kid.

00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:24.880
And yet the White House just keeps saying,
oh, he's kidding.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.970
He's kidding.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:30.900
This is borderline criminal and it's definitely
murderous.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.820
And I want to be sure that you have all of
the facts to understand this story.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.290
So I'm instead of going through this story,
however else I might do it.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.020
I'm going to go through the story chronologically
for you.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.020
OK.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.780
So the start of the story is the United States
failed on corona virus testing from day one

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.290
of the U.S. and South Korea got our first
cases at the same time within hours of each

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.290
other.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.960
We didn't develop a test quickly.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.600
We didn't roll out a test quickly.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.760
We didn't contact tracing isolate.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.210
South Korea did.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.520
They dominated the virus.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.680
We are leading in cases and deaths.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:10.079
So that's like the quick summary that gets
us to Saturday, Saturday at his Corona rally

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:12.310
in Tulsa, Oklahoma.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:18.710
Trump admitted for the first time I told them
to do less testing in order to find fewer

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:19.710
cases.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.909
This is from Saturday.

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:22.069
Test of what you do.

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:23.069
Testing.

00:01:23.069 --> 00:01:25.380
To that extent, you can find more people.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.530
You got to find more cases.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:32.070
So I said to my people, slowed the testing
down, please.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.369
They tests and they test.

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:36.040
We had tests that people don't know what's
going on.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.610
We got tests, we got another one over here.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.549
So this is, of course, completely outrageous.

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:47.639
It's a president admitting that for political
reasons, he asked for something that leads

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:49.619
to more death.

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:52.939
The White House reaction was he was just kidding.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:55.929
Spokes people said it was just a joke.

00:01:55.929 --> 00:01:59.170
Representatives said it was sarcasm.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:06.520
So then on Monday, Joe St. George interviews
Trump and asks him, did you order Corona virus

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.830
testing to be slowed down?

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.190
Trump doesn't really answer the question,
but he does say a lot of words.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.580
Take a look.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.569
On Saturday night, you said that you told
your staff to slow the testing down to improve

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:18.569
the numbers.

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:21.900
Does that mean someone watching this right
now on their local news is not going to get

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.900
a test?

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:23.900
Because you asked.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.870
We do more testing than any country in the
world by far.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.299
Twenty five million tests.

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:28.989
Other countries do one million.

00:02:28.989 --> 00:02:32.900
Every time you do a test, as you do more tests,
it shows more and more cases.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.260
So we're so far advanced both in terms of
the quality and the amount that we're doing

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.260
all these tests.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.260
And it shows cases.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.980
If other countries aren't doing or if we did
slow it down, we wouldn't show nearly as many

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.040
cases.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.140
So here, Trump doesn't deny that he asked
for less testing.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:54.520
He simply says if we did less testing, we'd
have fewer cases.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:03:00.440
And again, reporters ask the White House and
the Trump campaign that he really ordered

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.220
testing to be slowed down because he didn't
deny it.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.409
He was given the chance by Joe St George to
deny it, and he did not deny it.

00:03:07.409 --> 00:03:10.370
And the White House, again says it's a joke.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:14.239
The campaign says he was kidding, et cetera,
et cetera.

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:18.079
So finally yesterday, Donald Trump has asked
straight up.

00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:19.349
Were you kidding?

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:20.989
Because people are saying you were kidding.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:22.040
Were you kidding?

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:32.640
And Trump says, I don't kid.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.640
I don't get.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.000
Let me just tell you, let me make it clear.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.219
We have got the greatest testing program anywhere
in the world.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:44.359
So Trump goes into the same talking point
again.

00:03:44.359 --> 00:03:47.400
But the key phrase is, I don't kid.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.129
He was not kidding when he asked for testing
to be slowed down.

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:57.560
He was not kidding when he said that he asked
for testing to be slowed down.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:03.120
Are they also going to say that him saying
he doesn't kid was a form of kidding, like

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.011
what's left at this point from this crumbled
attempt, the defense of Donald Trump, he's

00:04:08.011 --> 00:04:10.510
given chance after chance.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:16.199
He's presented with opportunity after opportunity
to improve his answer like it's a do over,

00:04:16.199 --> 00:04:17.720
in a sense.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.320
And he just restates what he said on Saturday
night.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.500
He could clarify, oh, well, you know, I meant
this other thing.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.240
He doesn't change it at all because it's the
truth.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.050
It's like being allowed to retake a test.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:36.620
After you're given all the answers and you
still put down all the same wrong answers

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:42.970
from when you first took the test, I got an
e-mail saying, David, is this is this a confession

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:50.111
to negligent homicide? Trump is admitting
that he asked for something to be done, which

00:04:50.111 --> 00:04:53.060
he thought would be good politically.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.870
Which leads to more deaths.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.360
I mean, maybe I just don't even think this
is the right direction to go.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.949
Like, Trump is not going to be held criminally
liable in any way here.

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:06.930
We essentially have you know, I mean, it's
kind of depressing.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:12.919
But for for a couple years now, I've been
saying November 3rd, 2020, is when we will

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:16.169
have the opportunity to give him a consequence.

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:19.620
We're talking about him like he's a little
boy who's misbehaved because essentially that's

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.000
how he behaves.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.280
The it wasn't going to be the Russia investigation.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.110
It wasn't going to be impeachment.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:32.440
It's not going to be removal under the 25th
Amendment by his cabinet for being unfit.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:37.580
The opportunity for a consequence is November
3rd.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:43.220
And all of these disasters and tragedies are
valid reasons to remove him.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:06:16.910
And hopefully we will do it because it's really
the only opportunity

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:44.330
that

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:51.949
we have.

